# Agent shell for Rails commands

Gems are already installed. Do **not** run `bundle install`, `bundle update`, `gem install` for project deps, or `bin/setup` to "fix" Bundler in the agent shell.

The agent shell does not run mise's per-directory hook, so plain `ruby` resolves to the global Ruby (from `~/.config/mise/config.toml`), not the project's. Always go through `mise exec --`; versions come from `mise.toml`.

Cursor's sandbox can set `BUNDLE_PATH` to an empty cache. Unset it and request `all` permissions for Rails/test commands:

```bash
mise exec -- env -u BUNDLE_PATH bin/rails test test/path/to/test.rb
```

Same pattern for `bin/rubocop`, `bin/brakeman`, `bin/ci`, and other `bin/*` wrappers. Never switch Ruby/Node versions or edit `mise.toml` to make a command work.

Run tests freely. If it still fails after `mise exec -- env -u BUNDLE_PATH` + `all`, give the user the exact local command.
